cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "AmNat reproducibility skill: an AI agent helper for archiving data and code"
version: 0.9.0-beta
date-released: 2026-10-28
authors:
  - family-names: Brandvain
    given-names: Yaniv
    affiliation: University of Minnesota
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yanivjb/data_editor"
abstract: >-
  An agent skill for Claude Code and Codex that helps authors prepare data, code,
  and README files for submission. It checks a project against The American
  Naturalist's checklist for archiving data and code and reproducibility best
  practice, reruns the code in a fresh session, checks that every figure, table,
  and number in the manuscript is reproduced, and helps fix what the author
  chooses.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - data archiving
  - open science
  - ecology
  - evolution
  - AI agents
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A checklist for reproducible archiving data and code in ecology, evolution, and behavior"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bolnick
        given-names: Daniel I.
